-- title:
--   Number of cusps of Γ₀(N) equals sum_{d∣ N}φ(gcd(d,N/d))
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a natural number with $N \neq 0$. Consider the subgroup $\Gamma_0(N)$ of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, pushed forward along the map to $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q})$, so that `Gamma0Q N` is its image as a subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q})$; this group acts on the one-point compactification `OnePoint ℚ` of $\mathbb{Q}$, i.e. on $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Q})$ presented as $\mathbb{Q} \cup \{\infty\}$. The type [`ModularCurve.CuspSpace N`](def/ModularCurve_CuspSpace.html#L103) is the quotient of $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Q})$ by the orbit relation for this action, that is the set of cusps $\Gamma_0(N) \backslash \mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Q})$. The assertion is that the cardinality of this quotient, taken as a natural number via `Nat.card`, equals $$\mathrm{cuspCount}(N) = \sum_{d \mid N} \varphi\bigl(\gcd(d, N/d)\bigr),$$ the sum being over the positive divisors $d$ of $N$ and $\varphi$ the Euler totient function; in particular the quotient is finite, since `Nat.card` of an infinite type would be $0$ while the right-hand side is positive.
--
--   This is the classical count of the cusps of the modular curve $X_0(N)$, $\nu_\infty(N) = \sum_{d \mid N} \varphi(\gcd(d, N/d))$. It feeds the numerical input for the genus computations and related estimates for $X_0(N)$, being used for the count of orbits of the unipotent subgroup generated by $T$ and for the bound on the rank of the space of parabolic homomorphisms in terms of the genus formula.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_CuspSpace_card_cuspSpace_eq_cuspCount.lean

